---
// The nine section cards from the single-page build. They were <div>s calling
// switchTab(); they are now real links, which is the whole point of Phase 2 —
// a crawler could not follow an onclick, and a user could not bookmark one.
//
// premium.css turns this grid into a three-by-three index — ordinal, mark,
// name, rule — instead of a row of eight pills with the ninth orphaned onto a
// line of its own. The only markup that needed to change for it is two:
// the chevron (a link that travels on hover has to have something to travel,
// and it is decorative, so it is hidden from the accessibility tree), and the
// <br> inside each label — it existed to force a two-line pill, and in a row
// it breaks a name in an odd place. Hiding it in CSS was not an option: a
// removed <br> leaves no space behind, so "Admission<br>Process" rendered as
// "AdmissionProcess". The space is in the markup instead, in both the English
// and the Hindi label, so i18n.js swaps like for like. Classes,
// hrefs, IDs and the data-en/data-hi labels are untouched — build-verify
// counts these nine anchors and i18n.js reads those labels.
